Z||000002||bubbajoexx||12-15-2000||07:58 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula 18:<BR><B>Alot of discusion is done on 3800 and I was wondering what type of mounts you guys are using. I have read some sites where up to 3 mounts are used other sites just use on with a dog-bone. WHat is the best way to mount a 3800 to the craddle? I have been following the thread on torque struts for v8 and it seems like some guys running 3800 are saying they need a little extra bracing to controll the torque. Any thoughts?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>the best mount is the front mount from a 85 century t/type it is the same configuration as the fiero front mount  and it dose not need modifing to work.||||reg||6
Z||000003||terryk||12-15-2000||08:18 PM||||if the engine is a 92-95 Supercharged 3800, the bracket won't fit if you try to use the stock oil filter adapter. It will hit the bracket. In this case, you have to modify the adapter for an external filter. A Toronado adapter will work but it takes enough grinding that I dropped the idea.<P>The stock adapter hits the bracket and the other styles where the filter mounts higher hits a tensioner. <P>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
